<!-- DataTables library tags. Shared by datatables.ejs (results/fixture tables) and
     datatables-stats.ejs (stats tables) so the URLs are declared in one place.
     The bundle is DataTables + Buttons/ColVis + FixedHeader + Responsive; date-euro
     adds the dd/mm/yyyy sort type both partials rely on, and page.jumpToData() (used
     by datatables.ejs only) is loaded here too so the order below holds.

     Self-hosted in static/vendor/datatables/ since Oct 2026 (Stockport's HARD-45). From
     cdn.datatables.net these were three synchronous scripts and a render-blocking
     stylesheet on a host nothing else on the page used. They are byte-for-byte what the
     CDN's builder serves, not an npm install: the bundle is a builder output (rebuild
     link in its header) and the npm equivalent is several packages at different
     versions, which is an upgrade, not a move.

     The bundle has NO jQuery in it (no `jq-` segment in its builder URL). It used to
     include jQuery 3.3.1, fetched on top of footer.ejs's copy and then replacing
     window.jQuery with a second instance. Every view includes this AFTER
     include('footer.ejs', { useJQuery: true }), so footer's jQuery is defined by the time
     anything here runs — keep it that way.

     `defer` keeps document order, so the plug-ins run after the bundle they register
     on, and all of it before DOMContentLoaded — which is when jQuery's ready fires the
     inline initialisers in datatables.ejs and datatables-stats.ejs.
     test/integration/datatables-self-hosted.test.js pins all of this. -->
<script defer src="<%= assetUrl('/static/vendor/datatables/datatables.min.js') %>"></script>
<script defer src="<%= assetUrl('/static/vendor/datatables/date-euro.js') %>"></script>
<script defer src="<%= assetUrl('/static/vendor/datatables/page.jumpToData.js') %>"></script>
